pub(crate) static TEXTS: &[&str] = &[
    "---\nname: blocks\ndescription: Build a blocks screen as data: the kinds and their fields, the guard's rules, and example screens that pass them. Use it when writing or changing a screen.\n---\n\n# blocks\n\nA screen is data: a `screen` or `sheet` block of typed blocks, checked, then drawn by a renderer. Start a new screen from a page in `examples/` (each has no guard finding), build it from the kinds below, keep it clear of the rules in `rules.md`, and check it with `blocks check`. Setting up and reading the guard: `docs/guard.md` in the blocks repo.\n\n## Kinds\n\n- [`screen`](kinds/screen.md): A whole screen.\n- [`sheet`](kinds/sheet.md): A sheet over a screen.\n- [`section`](kinds/section.md): A titled group of blocks.\n- [`list`](kinds/list.md): A list of rows.\n- [`row`](kinds/row.md): One row of a list.\n- [`card`](kinds/card.md): A card: an ask, a run, a config or a proposal.\n- [`choice`](kinds/choice.md): A question with options, a free answer and a default.\n- [`form`](kinds/form.md): A form of fields; also the `config` kind.\n- [`config`](kinds/config.md): A form of fields; also the `config` kind.\n- [`secret`](kinds/secret.md): A secret's input: its value is never sent back.\n- [`run`](kinds/run.md): A command the owner approves to run.\n- [`button`](kinds/button.md): A button.\n- [`chips`](kinds/chips.md): A row of chips, one or many selected.\n- [`stat`](kinds/stat.md): Figures: a list of tiles, or one tile inline.\n- [`text`](kinds/text.md): Text: markdown, or a plain styled line.\n- [`images`](kinds/images.md): A strip of images.\n- [`web`](kinds/web.md): A web view of a fixed height.\n- [`diff`](kinds/diff.md): A file's diff.\n- [`editor`](kinds/editor.md): A text editor and its errors.\n- [`scene`](kinds/scene.md): Lanes at work.\n- [`diagram`](kinds/diagram.md): A diagram from its source, with counts and its nodes.\n- [`composer`](kinds/composer.md): A message box: its send action, its chips and the messages queued.\n- [`lines`](kinds/lines.md): Repeating rows of fields with add and remove, running totals and a balance check.\n- [`prose`](kinds/prose.md): Text as a tree of headings, paragraphs, lists, quotes and code.\n- [`hero`](kinds/hero.md): A page's opening: a title, a line, a picture and its actions.\n- [`media`](kinds/media.md): A picture or a video of a known size.\n- [`nav`](kinds/nav.md): A site's link bar.\n- [`island`](kinds/island.md): A client component the app hosts: its props in, its named events out.\n- [`table`](kinds/table.md): A data table: typed columns, rows by id, sort, filter, totals, row select and export.\n- [`steps`](kinds/steps.md): A stepper of named steps with its current one, or progress bars.\n- [`chart`](kinds/chart.md): A chart of named series over x values: bar, stacked, line, combo or donut.\n- [`toast`](kinds/toast.md): A short line after an action, in a tone, with an optional undo: an answer's toast, or drawn where it sits.\n- [`pages`](kinds/pages.md): A document as the app's server drew it, one picture a page: paged and zoomed in the view, with its PDF.\n- [`timeline`](kinds/timeline.md): Rows of bars on a day axis from `from` to `to` (ISO days); `move`, `stretch` and `draw` each send a `DaySpan`.\n\n## More\n\n- `rules.md`: every guard rule, what fires it and its fix\n- `examples/`: whole screens with no finding\n",
    "# `screen`\n\nA whole screen.\n\nThe Rust type `Screen`; in TS, `screen(fields: Screen)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `actions` | `Act[]` | optional |\n| `back` | `string` | optional |\n| `badge` | `number` | optional |\n| `blocks` | `Block[]` | optional |\n| `done` | `Submit` | optional |\n| `focus` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `large` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `locale` | `Locale` | optional |\n| `pending` | `Pending` | optional |\n| `personas` | `Record<string, unknown>[]` | optional |\n| `refresh` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `sites` | `number` | optional |\n| `source` | `string` | optional |\n| `state` | `Record<string, Lit>` | optional |\n| `stream` | `string` | optional |\n| `threads` | `Record<string, unknown>[]` | optional |\n| `title` | `string` | optional |\n| `url` | `string` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"screen\",\n  \"id\": \"home\",\n  \"title\": \"Home\",\n  \"state\": {\n    \"ready\": true\n  },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"id\": \"hint\",\n      \"markdown\": \"Ready\",\n      \"show\": {\n        \"get\": \"ready\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"screen\",\n  \"id\": \"home\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"Home\",\n  \"children\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"text\",\n      \"id\": \"hint\",\n      \"variant\": null,\n      \"drawn\": \"native\",\n      \"role\": \"group\",\n      \"name\": \"hint\",\n      \"children\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n",
    "# `sheet`\n\nA sheet over a screen.\n\nThe Rust type `Sheet`; in TS, `sheet(fields: Sheet)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `blocks` | `Block[]` | required |\n| `cancel` | `string` | optional |\n| `done` | `Submit` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `locale` | `Locale` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `title` | `string` | required |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"sheet\",\n  \"id\": \"add\",\n  \"title\": \"Add a repo\",\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"id\": \"sheet-note\",\n      \"markdown\": \"Pick one\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"sheet\",\n  \"id\": \"add\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"Add a repo\",\n  \"children\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"text\",\n      \"id\": \"sheet-note\",\n      \"variant\": null,\n      \"drawn\": \"native\",\n      \"role\": \"group\",\n      \"name\": \"sheet-note\",\n      \"children\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n",
    "# `section`\n\nA titled group of blocks.\n\nThe Rust type `Section`; in TS, `section(fields: Section)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `blocks` | `Block[]` | required |\n| `footer` | `string` | optional |\n| `header` | `string` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"section\",\n  \"id\": \"today\",\n  \"header\": \"Today\",\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"id\": \"today-note\",\n      \"markdown\": \"Quiet\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"section\",\n  \"id\": \"today\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"region\",\n  \"name\": \"Today\",\n  \"children\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"text\",\n      \"id\": \"today-note\",\n      \"variant\": null,\n      \"drawn\": \"native\",\n      \"role\": \"group\",\n      \"name\": \"today-note\",\n      \"children\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n",
    "# `list`\n\nA list of rows.\n\nThe Rust type `List`; in TS, `list(fields: List)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `more` | `More` | optional |\n| `reorder` | `Gesture` | optional |\n| `rows` | `Block[]` | required |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"list\",\n  \"id\": \"rows\",\n  \"rows\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"row\",\n      \"id\": \"row\",\n      \"title\": \"Build\",\n      \"subtitle\": \"green\",\n      \"value\": \"2m\",\n      \"rounds\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"r1\",\n          \"name\": \"impl\",\n          \"state\": \"done\",\n          \"summary\": \"pushed\",\n          \"tap\": {\n            \"url\": \"/runs/1\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"r2\",\n          \"name\": \"review 1\",\n          \"state\": \"needs\",\n          \"summary\": \"one finding\",\n          \"lane\": {\n            \"name\": \"rev-1\",\n            \"lines\": [\n              \"reading the diff\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"blocks\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"text\",\n              \"id\": \"finding\",\n              \"markdown\": \"Fix the test\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"links\": [\n            {\n              \"label\": \"verdict\",\n              \"tap\": {\n                \"url\": \"/verdict\"\n              }\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"list\",\n  \"id\": \"rows\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"rows\",\n  \"children\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"row\",\n      \"id\": \"row\",\n      \"variant\": null,\n      \"drawn\": \"native\",\n      \"role\": \"group\",\n      \"name\": \"Build\",\n      \"children\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"text\",\n          \"id\": \"finding\",\n          \"variant\": null,\n          \"drawn\": \"native\",\n          \"role\": \"group\",\n          \"name\": \"finding\",\n          \"children\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n",
    "# `row`\n\nOne row of a list.\n\nThe Rust type `Row`; in TS, `row(fields: Row)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `accessory` | `Accessory` | optional |\n| `badge` | `Label` | optional |\n| `button` | `Act` | optional |\n| `changed` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `figure` | `Figure` | optional |\n| `handle` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `indent` | `number` | optional |\n| `lifted` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `menu` | `Act[]` | optional |\n| `rounds` | `Round[]` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `sticky` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `style` | `RowStyle` | optional |\n| `subtitle` | `Toned` | optional |\n| `swipe` | `Act[]` | optional |\n| `tap` | `Tap` | optional |\n| `title` | `string` | required |\n| `value` | `Shown` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"row\",\n  \"id\": \"build\",\n  \"title\": \"Build\",\n  \"subtitle\": \"green\",\n  \"value\": \"2m\"\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"row\",\n  \"id\": \"build\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"Build\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `card`\n\nA card: an ask, a run, a config or a proposal.\n\nThe Rust type `Card`; in TS, `card(fields: Card)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `badge` | `Label` | optional |\n| `blocks` | `Block[]` | optional |\n| `buttons` | `Block[]` | optional |\n| `fold` | `Fold` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `kind` | `CardKind` | optional |\n| `menu` | `Act[]` | optional |\n| `meta` | `Shown` | optional |\n| `push` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `subtitle` | `Toned` | optional |\n| `tap` | `Tap` | optional |\n| `title` | `string` | optional |\n| `tone` | `Tone` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"card\",\n  \"id\": \"card\",\n  \"kind\": \"ask\",\n  \"title\": \"q1\",\n  \"subtitle\": \"waiting\",\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"since\": \"2026-11-09T09:35:00Z\",\n    \"label\": \"as of {} ago\"\n  },\n  \"badge\": {\n    \"text\": {\n      \"until\": \"2026-11-09T09:53:00Z\",\n      \"label\": \"lapses in {rel}\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"row\",\n      \"id\": \"card-row\",\n      \"title\": \"Review\",\n      \"subtitle\": {\n        \"text\": {\n          \"until\": \"2026-11-09T09:53:00Z\",\n          \"label\": \"decides in {rel}\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"value\": {\n        \"since\": \"2026-11-09T09:35:00Z\",\n        \"label\": \"{} ago\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"stat\",\n      \"id\": \"card-up\",\n      \"label\": \"up\",\n      \"value\": {\n        \"since\": \"2026-11-09T09:35:00Z\",\n        \"label\": \"{}\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"card\",\n  \"id\": \"card\",\n  \"variant\": \"ask\",\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"q1\",\n  \"children\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"row\",\n      \"id\": \"card-row\",\n      \"variant\": null,\n      \"drawn\": \"native\",\n      \"role\": \"group\",\n      \"name\": \"Review\",\n      \"children\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"stat\",\n      \"id\": \"card-up\",\n      \"variant\": null,\n      \"drawn\": \"native\",\n      \"role\": \"group\",\n      \"name\": \"up\",\n      \"children\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n",
    "# `choice`\n\nA question with options, a free answer and a default.\n\nThe Rust type `Choice`; in TS, `choice(fields: Choice)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `action` | `string` | required |\n| `default` | `ChoiceDefault` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `options` | `ChoiceOption[]` | required |\n| `other` | `Other` | optional |\n| `question` | `string` | optional |\n| `recommended` | `string` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `values` | `Record<string, unknown>` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"choice\",\n  \"id\": \"ask\",\n  \"action\": \"answer\",\n  \"question\": \"Merge it?\",\n  \"options\": [\n    {\n      \"value\": \"yes\",\n      \"label\": \"Yes\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"choice\",\n  \"id\": \"ask\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"Merge it?\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `form`\n\nA form of fields; also the `config` kind.\n\nThe Rust type `Form`; in TS, `form(fields: Form)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `action` | `string` | optional |\n| `fields` | `Field[]` | required |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `more` | `string` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `submit` | `Submit` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"form\",\n  \"id\": \"signup\",\n  \"action\": \"sign-up\",\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"name\": \"email\",\n      \"label\": \"Email\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"form\",\n  \"id\": \"signup\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"form\",\n  \"name\": \"signup\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `config`\n\nA form of fields; also the `config` kind.\n\nThe Rust type `Form`; in TS, `config(fields: Form)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `action` | `string` | optional |\n| `fields` | `Field[]` | required |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `more` | `string` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `submit` | `Submit` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"config\",\n  \"id\": \"settings\",\n  \"action\": \"save\",\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"name\": \"repo\",\n      \"label\": \"Repo\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"config\",\n  \"id\": \"settings\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"form\",\n  \"name\": \"settings\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `secret`\n\nA secret's input: its value is never sent back.\n\nThe Rust type `Secret`; in TS, `secret(fields: Secret)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `action` | `string` | required |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `label` | `string` | optional |\n| `name` | `string` | required |\n| `placeholder` | `string` | optional |\n| `set` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `values` | `Record<string, unknown>` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"secret\",\n  \"id\": \"token\",\n  \"name\": \"token\",\n  \"action\": \"save-token\",\n  \"label\": \"API token\"\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"secret\",\n  \"id\": \"token\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"API token\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `run`\n\nA command the owner approves to run.\n\nThe Rust type `Run`; in TS, `run(fields: Run)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `action` | `string` | required |\n| `command` | `string` | required |\n| `dir` | `string` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `sha` | `string` | required |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `touches` | `string` | optional |\n| `until` | `string` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"run\",\n  \"id\": \"run\",\n  \"action\": \"approve\",\n  \"command\": \"cargo test\",\n  \"sha\": \"4f2a9c1\",\n  \"dir\": \"crates\"\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"run\",\n  \"id\": \"run\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"cargo test\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `button`\n\nA button.\n\nThe Rust type `Button`; in TS, `button(fields: Button)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `action` | `string` | optional |\n| `confirm` | `Confirm` | optional |\n| `enabled` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `label` | `string` | required |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `style` | `ButtonStyle` | optional |\n| `tap` | `Tap` | optional |\n| `values` | `Record<string, unknown>` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"button\",\n  \"id\": \"save\",\n  \"label\": \"Save\",\n  \"action\": \"save\"\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"button\",\n  \"id\": \"save\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"button\",\n  \"name\": \"Save\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `chips`\n\nA row of chips, one or many selected.\n\nThe Rust type `Chips`; in TS, `chips(fields: Chips)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `action` | `string` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `multi` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `name` | `string` | required |\n| `options` | `ChipOption[]` | required |\n| `selected` | `string[]` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"chips\",\n  \"id\": \"effort\",\n  \"name\": \"effort\",\n  \"options\": [\n    {\n      \"value\": \"low\",\n      \"label\": \"low\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"value\": \"high\",\n      \"label\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"chips\",\n  \"id\": \"effort\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"effort\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `stat`\n\nFigures: a list of tiles, or one tile inline.\n\nThe Rust type `Stat`; in TS, `stat(fields: Stat)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `items` | `Tile[]` | optional |\n| `label` | `string` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `spark` | `number[]` | optional |\n| `tone` | `Tone` | optional |\n| `unit` | `string` | optional |\n| `value` | `Shown` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"stat\",\n  \"id\": \"open\",\n  \"label\": \"open\",\n  \"value\": 3\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"stat\",\n  \"id\": \"open\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"open\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `text`\n\nText: markdown, or a plain styled line.\n\nThe Rust type `Text`; in TS, `text(fields: Text)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `center` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `font` | `string` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `markdown` | `string` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `size` | `number` | optional |\n| `style` | `TextStyle` | optional |\n| `text` | `string` | optional |\n| `tone` | `Tone` | optional |\n| `top` | `number` | optional |\n| `until` | `string` | optional |\n| `weight` | `string` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"text\",\n  \"id\": \"note\",\n  \"markdown\": \"**Hello**\"\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"text\",\n  \"id\": \"note\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"note\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `images`\n\nA strip of images.\n\nThe Rust type `Images`; in TS, `images(fields: Images)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `items` | `Image[]` | required |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `size` | `ImageSize` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"images\",\n  \"id\": \"shots\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"src\": \"/media/a.png\",\n      \"alt\": \"a\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"images\",\n  \"id\": \"shots\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"shots\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `web`\n\nA web view of a fixed height.\n\nThe Rust type `Web`; in TS, `web(fields: Web)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `height` | `number` | required |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `src` | `string` | required |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"web\",\n  \"id\": \"doc\",\n  \"src\": \"/doc\",\n  \"height\": 240\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"web\",\n  \"id\": \"doc\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"doc\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `diff`\n\nA file's diff.\n\nThe Rust type `Diff`; in TS, `diff(fields: Diff)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `file` | `string` | required |\n| `hunks` | `Hunk[]` | required |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `summary` | `string` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"diff\",\n  \"id\": \"change\",\n  \"file\": \"src/lib.rs\",\n  \"hunks\": [\n    {\n      \"at\": \"@@ -1 +1 @@\",\n      \"lines\": [\n        \"-a\",\n        \"+b\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"diff\",\n  \"id\": \"change\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"src/lib.rs\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `editor`\n\nA text editor and its errors.\n\nThe Rust type `Editor`; in TS, `editor(fields: Editor)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `action` | `string` | required |\n| `errors` | `LineError[]` | optional |\n| `first` | `number` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `name` | `string` | required |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `text` | `string` | required |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"editor\",\n  \"id\": \"editor\",\n  \"name\": \"notes\",\n  \"text\": \"hello\",\n  \"action\": \"save-notes\"\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"editor\",\n  \"id\": \"editor\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"button\",\n  \"name\": \"notes\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `scene`\n\nLanes at work.\n\nThe Rust type `Scene`; in TS, `scene(fields: Scene)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `label` | `string` | optional |\n| `lanes` | `Lane[]` | optional |\n| `load` | `Load` | optional |\n| `repos` | `SceneRepo[]` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `weather` | `Weather` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"scene\",\n  \"id\": \"scene\",\n  \"label\": \"lanes\",\n  \"lanes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"impl-1\",\n      \"title\": \"impl\",\n      \"state\": \"working\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"scene\",\n  \"id\": \"scene\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"lanes\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `diagram`\n\nA diagram from its source, with counts and its nodes.\n\nThe Rust type `Diagram`; in TS, `diagram(fields: Diagram)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `counts` | `Record<string, number>` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `nodes` | `Nodes` | optional |\n| `selected` | `string` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `source` | `string` | required |\n| `title` | `string` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"diagram\",\n  \"id\": \"flow\",\n  \"title\": \"Flow\",\n  \"source\": \"[*] --> a\\na --> b\"\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"diagram\",\n  \"id\": \"flow\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"Flow\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `composer`\n\nA message box: its send action, its chips and the messages queued.\n\nThe Rust type `Composer`; in TS, `composer(fields: Composer)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `action` | `string` | required |\n| `acts` | `Record<string, string>` | optional |\n| `chips` | `ComposerChip[]` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `label` | `string` | optional |\n| `placeholder` | `string` | optional |\n| `queued` | `Queued[]` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `values` | `Record<string, unknown>` | optional |\n| `working` | `Working` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"composer\",\n  \"id\": \"say\",\n  \"action\": \"say\",\n  \"placeholder\": \"message the team\"\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"composer\",\n  \"id\": \"say\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"message the team\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `lines`\n\nRepeating rows of fields with add and remove, running totals and a balance check.\n\nThe Rust type `Lines`; in TS, `lines(fields: Lines)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `action` | `string` | optional |\n| `add` | `string` | optional |\n| `balance` | `string[]` | optional |\n| `calc` | `Record<string, Expr>` | optional |\n| `columns` | `Field[]` | required |\n| `empty` | `string` | optional |\n| `errors` | `RowError[]` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `items` | `LineItem[]` | required |\n| `label` | `string` | optional |\n| `max` | `number` | optional |\n| `min` | `number` | optional |\n| `name` | `string` | required |\n| `scale` | `number` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `submit` | `Submit` | optional |\n| `sum` | `string[]` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"lines\",\n  \"id\": \"journal\",\n  \"name\": \"lines\",\n  \"label\": \"journal lines\",\n  \"action\": \"check-journal\",\n  \"columns\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"picker\",\n      \"name\": \"account\",\n      \"label\": \"Account\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"6100 Rent\",\n        \"6200 Utilities\",\n        \"2100 Payables\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"name\": \"memo\",\n      \"label\": \"Description\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"name\": \"debit\",\n      \"label\": \"Debit\",\n      \"keyboard\": \"number\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"name\": \"credit\",\n      \"label\": \"Credit\",\n      \"keyboard\": \"number\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"l1\",\n      \"values\": {\n        \"account\": \"6100 Rent\",\n        \"debit\": \"2400\",\n        \"memo\": \"office rent\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"l2\",\n      \"values\": {\n        \"account\": \"\",\n        \"debit\": \"318.40\",\n        \"memo\": \"power and water\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"l3\",\n      \"values\": {\n        \"account\": \"2100 Payables\",\n        \"credit\": \"2668.50\",\n        \"memo\": \"landlord\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sum\": [\n    \"debit\",\n    \"credit\"\n  ],\n  \"balance\": [\n    \"debit\",\n    \"credit\"\n  ],\n  \"min\": 2,\n  \"add\": \"add line\",\n  \"errors\": [\n    {\n      \"row\": \"l2\",\n      \"name\": \"account\",\n      \"message\": \"pick an account for line 2\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"submit\": {\n    \"label\": \"post entry\",\n    \"action\": \"post-journal\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"lines\",\n  \"id\": \"journal\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"journal lines\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `prose`\n\nText as a tree of headings, paragraphs, lists, quotes and code.\n\nThe Rust type `Prose`; in TS, `prose(fields: Prose)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `parts` | `Part[]` | required |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"prose\",\n  \"id\": \"about\",\n  \"parts\": [\n    {\n      \"part\": \"heading\",\n      \"level\": 2,\n      \"spans\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Blocks\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"part\": \"para\",\n      \"spans\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Typed \"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"screens\",\n          \"bold\": true\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"part\": \"list\",\n      \"ordered\": false,\n      \"items\": [\n        [\n          {\n            \"text\": \"one\"\n          }\n        ],\n        [\n          {\n            \"text\": \"two\"\n          }\n        ]\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"part\": \"quote\",\n      \"spans\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Built by type.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"part\": \"code\",\n      \"lang\": \"rust\",\n      \"text\": \"Row::new(\\\"a\\\")\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"part\": \"rule\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"prose\",\n  \"id\": \"about\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"about\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `hero`\n\nA page's opening: a title, a line, a picture and its actions.\n\nThe Rust type `Hero`; in TS, `hero(fields: Hero)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `actions` | `Act[]` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `media` | `Media` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `subtitle` | `string` | optional |\n| `title` | `string` | required |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"hero\",\n  \"id\": \"hero\",\n  \"title\": \"Blocks\",\n  \"subtitle\": \"One shape, three renderers\",\n  \"media\": {\n    \"src\": \"/media/chart.png\",\n    \"alt\": \"a bar chart\",\n    \"width\": 640,\n    \"height\": 360,\n    \"caption\": \"This week\"\n  },\n  \"actions\": [\n    {\n      \"label\": \"Start\",\n      \"action\": \"start\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"hero\",\n  \"id\": \"hero\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"Blocks\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `media`\n\nA picture or a video of a known size.\n\nThe Rust type `Media`; in TS, `media(fields: Media)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `alt` | `string` | required |\n| `caption` | `string` | optional |\n| `draw` | `Gesture` | optional |\n| `height` | `number` | required |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `marks` | `Mark[]` | optional |\n| `move` | `Gesture` | optional |\n| `poster` | `string` | optional |\n| `remove` | `Gesture` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `src` | `string` | required |\n| `stretch` | `Gesture` | optional |\n| `tools` | `MarkKind[]` | optional |\n| `video` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `width` | `number` | required |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"media\",\n  \"id\": \"chart\",\n  \"src\": \"/media/chart.png\",\n  \"alt\": \"a bar chart\",\n  \"width\": 640,\n  \"height\": 360,\n  \"caption\": \"This week\",\n  \"marks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"peak\",\n      \"kind\": \"highlight\",\n      \"at\": [\n        0.5,\n        0.2\n      ],\n      \"to\": [\n        0.62,\n        0.9\n      ],\n      \"tone\": \"warn\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"arrow\",\n      \"kind\": \"arrow\",\n      \"at\": [\n        0.3,\n        0.15\n      ],\n      \"to\": [\n        0.48,\n        0.3\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"note\",\n      \"kind\": \"text\",\n      \"at\": [\n        0.05,\n        0.08\n      ],\n      \"text\": \"Release week\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dip\",\n      \"kind\": \"pin\",\n      \"at\": [\n        0.78,\n        0.7\n      ],\n      \"text\": \"1\",\n      \"tone\": \"info\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"media\",\n  \"id\": \"chart\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"a bar chart\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `nav`\n\nA site's link bar.\n\nThe Rust type `Nav`; in TS, `nav(fields: Nav)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `brand` | `NavLink` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `links` | `NavLink[]` | required |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"nav\",\n  \"id\": \"nav\",\n  \"brand\": {\n    \"label\": \"Blocks\",\n    \"href\": \"/\"\n  },\n  \"links\": [\n    {\n      \"label\": \"Docs\",\n      \"href\": \"/docs\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"nav\",\n  \"id\": \"nav\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"navigation\",\n  \"name\": \"nav\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `island`\n\nA client component the app hosts: its props in, its named events out.\n\nThe Rust type `Island`; in TS, `island(fields: Island)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `events` | `string[]` | optional |\n| `fallback` | `Fallback` | required |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `name` | `string` | required |\n| `props` | `Record<string, unknown>` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `size` | `IslandSize` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"island\",\n  \"id\": \"map\",\n  \"name\": \"x-map\",\n  \"fallback\": {\n    \"title\": \"The map\"\n  },\n  \"props\": {\n    \"zoom\": 3\n  },\n  \"events\": [\n    \"pick\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"island\",\n  \"id\": \"map\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"x-map\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `table`\n\nA data table: typed columns, rows by id, sort, filter, totals, row select and export.\n\nThe Rust type `Table`; in TS, `table(fields: Table)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `calc` | `Record<string, Expr>` | optional |\n| `columns` | `Column[]` | required |\n| `edit` | `Gesture` | optional |\n| `empty` | `string` | optional |\n| `export` | `ExportFormat[]` | optional |\n| `filter` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `more` | `Page` | optional |\n| `reorder` | `Gesture` | optional |\n| `rows` | `TableRow[]` | required |\n| `select` | `TableSelect` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `sort` | `TableSort` | optional |\n| `title` | `string` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"table\",\n  \"id\": \"invoices\",\n  \"title\": \"Invoices\",\n  \"columns\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"inv\",\n      \"label\": \"Invoice\",\n      \"kind\": \"text\",\n      \"phone\": \"meta\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"client\",\n      \"label\": \"Client\",\n      \"kind\": \"text\",\n      \"width\": 18,\n      \"phone\": \"title\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"status\",\n      \"label\": \"Status\",\n      \"kind\": \"tone\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"due\",\n      \"label\": \"Due\",\n      \"kind\": \"date\",\n      \"era\": \"be\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"late\",\n      \"label\": \"Overdue\",\n      \"kind\": \"bar\",\n      \"unit\": \"days\",\n      \"digits\": 0,\n      \"max\": 60,\n      \"tone\": \"warn\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"amount\",\n      \"label\": \"Amount\",\n      \"kind\": \"money\",\n      \"currency\": \"THB\",\n      \"total\": \"sum\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rows\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"INV-0133\",\n      \"cells\": {\n        \"amount\": 48750,\n        \"client\": \"Orchard Lane Clinic\",\n        \"due\": \"2026-10-18\",\n        \"inv\": \"INV-0133\",\n        \"late\": 32,\n        \"status\": {\n          \"text\": \"overdue\",\n          \"tone\": \"warn\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"tap\": {\n        \"open\": \"/invoice/INV-0133\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"INV-0136\",\n      \"cells\": {\n        \"amount\": 31500,\n        \"client\": \"Bluepeak Logistics\",\n        \"due\": \"2026-11-05\",\n        \"inv\": \"INV-0136\",\n        \"late\": 14,\n        \"status\": {\n          \"text\": \"disputed\",\n          \"tone\": \"bad\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"tap\": {\n        \"open\": \"/invoice/INV-0136\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"INV-0138\",\n      \"cells\": {\n        \"amount\": 18000,\n        \"client\": \"Saffron & Salt\",\n        \"due\": \"2026-11-19\",\n        \"inv\": \"INV-0138\",\n        \"status\": {\n          \"text\": \"sent\",\n          \"tone\": \"done\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"tap\": {\n        \"open\": \"/invoice/INV-0138\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"INV-0139\",\n      \"cells\": {\n        \"amount\": 15000,\n        \"client\": \"Tidewater Bakery\",\n        \"due\": \"2026-11-26\",\n        \"inv\": \"INV-0139\",\n        \"status\": {\n          \"text\": \"paid\",\n          \"tone\": \"ok\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"tap\": {\n        \"open\": \"/invoice/INV-0139\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"INV-0143\",\n      \"cells\": {\n        \"amount\": 13500,\n        \"client\": \"Moss Hill School\",\n        \"inv\": \"INV-0143\",\n        \"status\": {\n          \"text\": \"draft\",\n          \"tone\": \"mute\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"tap\": {\n        \"open\": \"/invoice/INV-0143\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sort\": {\n    \"by\": \"due\",\n    \"dir\": \"asc\"\n  },\n  \"empty\": \"No invoices yet.\",\n  \"select\": {\n    \"actions\": [\n      {\n        \"action\": \"remind\",\n        \"label\": \"send reminder\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"action\": \"void\",\n        \"label\": \"void\",\n        \"bad\": true\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"export\": [\n    \"csv\",\n    \"xlsx\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"table\",\n  \"id\": \"invoices\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"Invoices\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `steps`\n\nA stepper of named steps with its current one, or progress bars.\n\nThe Rust type `Steps`; in TS, `steps(fields: Steps)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `bars` | `Bar[]` | optional |\n| `current` | `string` | optional |\n| `done` | `boolean` | optional |\n| `fallback` | `Fallback` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `steps` | `Stage[]` | optional |\n| `title` | `string` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"steps\",\n  \"id\": \"stop\",\n  \"title\": \"Stop 3 of 8\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"stop\",\n      \"label\": \"Stop\",\n      \"sub\": \"arrived 09:42\",\n      \"tap\": {\n        \"open\": \"stop\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"lines\",\n      \"label\": \"Lines\",\n      \"sub\": \"6 checked\",\n      \"tap\": {\n        \"open\": \"lines\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"done\": true\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"steps\",\n  \"id\": \"stop\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"Stop 3 of 8\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `chart`\n\nA chart of named series over x values: bar, stacked, line, combo or donut.\n\nThe Rust type `Chart`; in TS, `chart(fields: Chart)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `chart` | `ChartKind` | required |\n| `empty` | `string` | optional |\n| `era` | `Era` | optional |\n| `format` | `ChartFormat` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `lang` | `string` | optional |\n| `selected` | `string` | optional |\n| `series` | `Series[]` | required |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `tap` | `Tap` | optional |\n| `title` | `string` | required |\n| `x` | `string[]` | required |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"chart\",\n  \"id\": \"revenue\",\n  \"title\": \"Revenue and target\",\n  \"chart\": \"combo\",\n  \"x\": [\n    \"2024-01\",\n    \"2024-02\",\n    \"2024-03\",\n    \"2024-04\",\n    \"2024-05\",\n    \"2024-06\"\n  ],\n  \"series\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Revenue\",\n      \"values\": [\n        11100000,\n        10600000,\n        12900000,\n        11800000,\n        12200000,\n        11400000\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Target\",\n      \"values\": [\n        11000000,\n        11000000,\n        12000000,\n        12000000,\n        12000000,\n        12500000\n      ],\n      \"tone\": \"warn\",\n      \"as\": \"line\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"era\": \"be\",\n  \"format\": \"thb_m\",\n  \"selected\": \"2024-03\",\n  \"tap\": {\n    \"action\": \"sales.month\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"chart\",\n  \"id\": \"revenue\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"figure\",\n  \"name\": \"Revenue and target\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `toast`\n\nA short line after an action, in a tone, with an optional undo: an answer's toast, or drawn where it sits.\n\nThe Rust type `Toast`; in TS, `toast(fields: Toast)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `fallback` | `Fallback` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `title` | `string` | required |\n| `tone` | `Tone` | optional |\n| `undo` | `Undo` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"toast\",\n  \"id\": \"archived\",\n  \"tone\": \"ok\",\n  \"title\": \"Archived 3 orders\",\n  \"undo\": {\n    \"action\": \"unarchive\",\n    \"values\": {\n      \"ids\": [\n        \"o-4821\",\n        \"o-4822\",\n        \"o-4825\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"toast\",\n  \"id\": \"archived\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"status\",\n  \"name\": \"Archived 3 orders\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `pages`\n\nA document as the app's server drew it, one picture a page: paged and zoomed in the view, with its PDF.\n\nThe Rust type `Pages`; in TS, `pages(fields: Pages)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `fallback` | `Fallback` | optional |\n| `file` | `string` | optional |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `note` | `string` | optional |\n| `pages` | `PageImage[]` | required |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `title` | `string` | optional |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"pages\",\n  \"id\": \"quote\",\n  \"title\": \"Q-2026-0418 rev 3\",\n  \"pages\": [\n    {\n      \"src\": \"/q/0418/1.png\",\n      \"alt\": \"Cover and priced items: 8 lines, total 51,092.50 including VAT\",\n      \"width\": 1240,\n      \"height\": 1754\n    },\n    {\n      \"src\": \"/q/0418/2.png\",\n      \"alt\": \"Terms and conditions, clauses 1 to 6\",\n      \"width\": 1240,\n      \"height\": 1754\n    },\n    {\n      \"src\": \"/q/0418/3.png\",\n      \"alt\": \"Programme of works and the acceptance signature box\",\n      \"width\": 1240,\n      \"height\": 1754\n    }\n  ],\n  \"file\": \"/q/0418.pdf\",\n  \"note\": \"Out of date: the prices changed after this was drawn.\"\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"pages\",\n  \"id\": \"quote\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"Q-2026-0418 rev 3\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# `timeline`\n\nRows of bars on a day axis from `from` to `to` (ISO days); `move`, `stretch` and `draw` each send a `DaySpan`.\n\nThe Rust type `Timeline`; in TS, `timeline(fields: Timeline)` from `web/src/gen/builders.ts`.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `draw` | `Gesture` | optional |\n| `empty` | `string` | optional |\n| `from` | `string` | required |\n| `id` | `string` | optional |\n| `move` | `Gesture` | optional |\n| `off` | `string[]` | optional |\n| `show` | `Expr` | optional |\n| `stretch` | `Gesture` | optional |\n| `title` | `string` | optional |\n| `to` | `string` | required |\n| `tracks` | `TimeRow[]` | required |\n\n## A sample\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"timeline\",\n  \"id\": \"plan\",\n  \"title\": \"Crews\",\n  \"from\": \"2026-12-01\",\n  \"to\": \"2026-12-31\",\n  \"off\": [\n    \"2026-12-05\",\n    \"2026-12-06\",\n    \"2026-12-10\",\n    \"2026-12-12\",\n    \"2026-12-13\",\n    \"2026-12-19\",\n    \"2026-12-20\",\n    \"2026-12-26\",\n    \"2026-12-27\",\n    \"2026-12-31\"\n  ],\n  \"tracks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"j0\",\n      \"title\": \"St Anne's annexe\",\n      \"subtitle\": \"Crew 3 · fit-out\",\n      \"bars\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b01\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-11-23\",\n          \"end\": \"2026-12-04\",\n          \"label\": \"Fit-out\",\n          \"progress\": 80\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"j1\",\n      \"title\": \"Riverside Tower A\",\n      \"subtitle\": \"Crew 1\",\n      \"bars\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b11\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-12-01\",\n          \"end\": \"2026-12-04\",\n          \"label\": \"Formwork\",\n          \"tone\": \"ok\",\n          \"progress\": 100\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b12\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-12-07\",\n          \"end\": \"2026-12-09\",\n          \"label\": \"Pour\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b13\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-12-14\",\n          \"end\": \"2026-12-22\",\n          \"label\": \"Cure\",\n          \"tone\": \"info\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"j2\",\n      \"title\": \"Riverside Tower B\",\n      \"subtitle\": \"Crew 2\",\n      \"bars\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b21\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-12-02\",\n          \"end\": \"2026-12-08\",\n          \"label\": \"Excavate\",\n          \"progress\": 60\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b22\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-12-11\",\n          \"end\": \"2026-12-18\",\n          \"label\": \"Footings\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"j3\",\n      \"title\": \"Marlow Street flats\",\n      \"subtitle\": \"Crew 3 · behind\",\n      \"bars\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b31\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-12-07\",\n          \"end\": \"2026-12-23\",\n          \"label\": \"Brickwork\",\n          \"tone\": \"warn\",\n          \"progress\": 30\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b32\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-12-28\",\n          \"end\": \"2026-12-28\",\n          \"label\": \"Inspect\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"j4\",\n      \"title\": \"Kingfisher school hall\",\n      \"subtitle\": \"Crew 1 · finished\",\n      \"bars\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b41\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-12-01\",\n          \"end\": \"2026-12-03\",\n          \"label\": \"Roof\",\n          \"tone\": \"ok\",\n          \"progress\": 100,\n          \"fixed\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b42\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-12-07\",\n          \"end\": \"2026-12-08\",\n          \"label\": \"Snag list\",\n          \"progress\": 100,\n          \"fixed\": true\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"j5\",\n      \"title\": \"Quayside car park\",\n      \"subtitle\": \"Crew 4\",\n      \"bars\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b51\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-12-15\",\n          \"end\": \"2026-12-18\",\n          \"label\": \"Resurface · no permit\",\n          \"tone\": \"bad\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b52\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-12-21\",\n          \"end\": \"2026-12-22\",\n          \"label\": \"Lines\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"j6\",\n      \"title\": \"Old Mill conversion\",\n      \"subtitle\": \"unassigned\",\n      \"bars\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"j7\",\n      \"title\": \"Pier Road drainage\",\n      \"subtitle\": \"Crew 2\",\n      \"bars\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b71\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-12-21\",\n          \"end\": \"2026-12-23\",\n          \"label\": \"Survey\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"b72\",\n          \"start\": \"2026-12-28\",\n          \"end\": \"2027-01-08\",\n          \"label\": \"Dig\",\n          \"tone\": \"accent\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"move\": {\n    \"action\": \"schedule\",\n    \"name\": \"bar\"\n  },\n  \"stretch\": {\n    \"action\": \"schedule\",\n    \"name\": \"bar\"\n  },\n  \"draw\": {\n    \"action\": \"schedule\",\n    \"name\": \"bar\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## The tree it draws\n\n```json\n{\n  \"kind\": \"timeline\",\n  \"id\": \"plan\",\n  \"variant\": null,\n  \"drawn\": \"native\",\n  \"role\": \"group\",\n  \"name\": \"Crews\",\n  \"children\": []\n}\n```\n",
    "# The guard's rules\n\nGuard version 2. A new error fails `blocks check`; a warning never fails.\n\n| rule | severity | since | fires on | fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `lint/action-no-id` | warn | 1 | a block that sends an action has no id | Give the block an `id`; tests, the harness and explore find it by id. |\n| `lint/actions-many` | warn | 1 | more than 12 actions on a screen, the rows' own not counted | Move the rare actions into a `menu` or a sheet. |\n| `guard/baseline-grew` | error | 1 | a baseline gained an entry for a rule older than the file | Fix the finding, or add an ignore with a reason. |\n| `guard/baseline-stale` | error | 1 | a baseline entry is no longer found | Run `blocks check --tighten`. |\n| `lint/buttons-many` | error | 1 | more than 3 buttons in one group | Keep up to three; move the rest into a `menu`. |\n| `render/clipped-text` | error | 2 | text is cut by its box with no ellipsis | Let the text wrap, or shorten it. |\n| `render/console` | error | 1 | a console error or an uncaught exception | Fix the script error; the message is in the finding. |\n| `render/contrast` | error | 2 | text under 4.5:1 against what is drawn behind it (3:1 from 24 px, or 18.66 px bold); text over an image is skipped and counted | Use a token pair the scheme gate passes: `--fg` on `--bg`, or a tone's own pair. |\n| `lint/depth` | error | 1 | blocks nested deeper than 6 | Flatten it: open the inner part as a sheet or a screen of its own with `tap.open`. |\n| `lint/destructive-unconfirmed` | error | 1 | a destructive button or act sends an action with no confirm | Add a `confirm` whose title names what is lost. |\n| `render/dropped` | warn | 2 | an island sent an event its `events` does not name | Name the event in the island's `events`, or stop sending it. |\n| `lint/empty-state` | error | 1 | a list with no rows or a section with no blocks, and no visible text, prose, hero or card beside it | Add a `text` beside it that says what will appear here. |\n| `explore/error-screen` | error | 1 | an answer is an error, its ops do not apply, or the screen they give has a fault | Answer with ops that apply to the screen as it is; `Built::check` the result. |\n| `lint/fault` | error | 1 | Built::check returns a fault | Build the block with its typed constructor; `Built::check` must return nothing. |\n| `css/fixed-width` | error | 2 | a `width` or `min-width` over 390 px | Use `max-width`, or a width in `%`. |\n| `render/frame-budget` | warn | 1 | first paint over 300 ms, or a frame over 16.7 ms | Draw fewer blocks at first: page the list, or fold the rest. |\n| `lint/island-unsized` | warn | 1 | an island with no size | Reserve its box with `size`, so the page does not jump when it loads. |\n| `lint/label-empty` | error | 1 | a blank button, act, chip, option or field label, or row title | Give it a label of one to three words. |\n| `lint/label-long` | error | 1 | a button, act or chip label over 30 characters, or a badge over 20 | Shorten it to a verb and its object; move the rest to a `confirm` or a `text` block. |\n| `lint/label-twice` | error | 1 | two buttons or acts in one group with one label and different actions | Rename one so that each says what it does. |\n| `lint/level-blocks` | warn | 1 | more than 12 blocks in one level, rows not counted | Group them into sections, or split the screen. |\n| `css/motion` | error | 2 | a transition or keyframe of anything but `transform` and `opacity` | Animate `transform` or `opacity` only. |\n| `render/no-name` | error | 2 | an actionable element or image with no accessible name | Give it a label, or an `alt` for an image. |\n| `render/no-size` | error | 2 | a drawn block has no width or no height | Give the block content, or hide it with `show`. |\n| `render/overflow` | error | 2 | a block leaves the 390 px width, or the page scrolls sideways | Let the block wrap: remove the fixed width or the unbroken text that holds it open. |\n| `render/overlap` | error | 2 | two sibling blocks cover each other | Remove the app rule that positions the block; let the layout place it. |\n| `lint/primary-twice` | error | 1 | two primary buttons among one block's children, or one at the top of a screen that has done | Keep one primary action in a group; make the others `plain`. |\n| `css/private-selector` | error | 2 | an app selector names a `.b-` class that is no generated hook | Style a hook from the renderer contract (`.b-<kind>`, `.b-<kind>__<part>`, `[data-variant]`, `[data-tone]`). |\n| `css/raw-colour` | error | 2 | an app colour property set to anything but a scheme token (`var(--fg)`, `var(--card)`, …), `currentColor`, `transparent` or `inherit` | Use the scheme token for that role, or add the colour to the app's scheme so the gate checks it. |\n| `guard/seed-missing` | warn | 1 | a screen with a list has no `empty` fixture, or no `long` one | Add the fixture from the app's fixture writer. |\n| `explore/sent-differs` | error | 1 | the renderer sent other actions than the screen declares for the step | Send the action from the block that declares it; an app view posts through the `act` it is handed. |\n| `render/tap-target` | error | 2 | a control under 44 by 44 px; a link inside running text is exempt | Give the control at least 44 px each way: use the kind's own button, or drop the app rule that shrinks it. |\n| `lint/text-wall` | warn | 1 | a text block's markdown over 600 characters | Use `prose`, or split it under section headers. |\n| `lint/title-long` | error | 1 | a title, header or question over 60 characters | Shorten it to 60 characters or fewer; move the detail to `subtitle` or to a `text` block. |\n| `render/tree` | error | 2 | the drawn tree is not the one the crate expects: a block missing, or a fallback where a view was expected | Register the kind's view, or send a kind this renderer draws. |\n| `render/truncated` | warn | 2 | a title or label ends in an ellipsis | Shorten it, or let it take two lines. |\n| `explore/unanswered` | error | 1 | the answerer gave no answer to an action the screen declares | Handle the action in the app, or remove the control. |\n| `explore/unstable` | error | 1 | the answerer gave another answer to the same walk | Make the answerer a function of its seed and the actions so far. |\n| `lint/untitled` | warn | 1 | a screen with no title | Give the screen a title of one to three words. |\n| `guard/unused-ignore` | error | 1 | an ignore matches no finding | Delete the ignore. |\n",
    "# Example: `ok-queue`\n\nA screen with no guard finding: start a new screen from it.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"actions\": [\n    {\n      \"action\": \"refresh\",\n      \"label\": \"Refresh\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"buttons\": [\n        {\n          \"action\": \"drive\",\n          \"id\": \"drive-now\",\n          \"label\": \"Drive now\",\n          \"style\": \"primary\",\n          \"type\": \"button\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"action\": \"pause\",\n          \"id\": \"pause\",\n          \"label\": \"Pause\",\n          \"type\": \"button\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"id\": \"drive\",\n      \"title\": \"Drive\",\n      \"type\": \"card\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"blocks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"rows\",\n          \"rows\": [\n            {\n              \"badge\": {\n                \"text\": \"impl\"\n              },\n              \"id\": \"r1\",\n              \"tap\": {\n                \"action\": \"open\"\n              },\n              \"title\": \"#159 guard lint\",\n              \"type\": \"row\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"button\": {\n                \"action\": \"stop\",\n                \"confirm\": {\n                  \"destructive\": true,\n                  \"ok\": \"Stop\",\n                  \"title\": \"Stop lane #160?\"\n                },\n                \"label\": \"Stop\",\n                \"tone\": \"bad\"\n              },\n              \"id\": \"r2\",\n              \"title\": \"#160 blocks check\",\n              \"type\": \"row\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"list\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"header\": \"Lanes\",\n      \"id\": \"lanes\",\n      \"type\": \"section\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"blocks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"merged\",\n          \"rows\": [],\n          \"type\": \"list\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"markdown\": \"Merged issues appear here.\",\n          \"type\": \"text\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"header\": \"Done\",\n      \"id\": \"done\",\n      \"type\": \"section\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fallback\": {\n        \"title\": \"Fleet map\"\n      },\n      \"id\": \"map\",\n      \"name\": \"fleet-map\",\n      \"size\": {\n        \"height\": 200,\n        \"width\": 358\n      },\n      \"type\": \"island\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"remove\",\n      \"confirm\": {\n        \"destructive\": true,\n        \"ok\": \"Remove\",\n        \"title\": \"Remove the fleet and its queue?\"\n      },\n      \"id\": \"rm\",\n      \"label\": \"Remove fleet\",\n      \"style\": \"destructive\",\n      \"type\": \"button\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"s\",\n  \"title\": \"Queue\",\n  \"type\": \"screen\"\n}\n```\n",
    "# Example: `ok-scan`\n\nA screen with no guard finding: start a new screen from it.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"fields\": [\n        {\n          \"label\": \"Signed for by\",\n          \"name\": \"who\",\n          \"type\": \"text\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"checks\": [\n            {\n              \"ok\": {\n                \"is\": {\n                  \"pattern\": \"filled\",\n                  \"value\": {\n                    \"get\": \"note\"\n                  }\n                }\n              },\n              \"say\": \"Scan the signed note\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"label\": \"Delivery note\",\n          \"max\": 5,\n          \"name\": \"note\",\n          \"type\": \"scan\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"id\": \"proof\",\n      \"submit\": {\n        \"action\": \"deliver\",\n        \"label\": \"Send\"\n      },\n      \"type\": \"form\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"delivery\",\n  \"title\": \"Delivery\",\n  \"type\": \"screen\"\n}\n```\n",
    "# Example: `ok-sheet`\n\nA screen with no guard finding: start a new screen from it.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"action\": \"add\",\n      \"fields\": [\n        {\n          \"label\": \"Repo\",\n          \"name\": \"repo\",\n          \"type\": \"text\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"id\": \"f\",\n      \"type\": \"form\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"cancel\",\n      \"id\": \"cancel-add\",\n      \"label\": \"Cancel\",\n      \"type\": \"button\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"done\": {\n    \"action\": \"add\",\n    \"label\": \"Add\"\n  },\n  \"id\": \"add\",\n  \"title\": \"Add fleet\",\n  \"type\": \"sheet\"\n}\n```\n",
];
